# rollback-round.allowed-errors — expected error-class lines during the
# partition/heal cycles this round deliberately provokes.               (#1040)
#
# One extended-regex per line; blank lines and full-line '#' comments are
# ignored (inline trailing comments are NOT supported by
# lib/expect-log-errors.sh's parser — never put a comment after a pattern on
# the same line, it becomes part of the regex). Consumed by
# assert_no_other_errors, which only classifies lines matching the shared
# LOG_ERROR_PATTERN in .claude/skills/devnet-validate/scripts/lib/
# log-level-counts.sh — a literal ' ERROR ' token, a panic, or one of the
# three invalid-block trace names. WARN/INFO lines (including both dugite
# fork-too-deep lines below) are already outside that classifier and do not
# strictly need an entry here; they are listed anyway as defense-in-depth
# against a future severity bump, and because rollback-round.sh's own
# comments point back to this file as the place that documents them.

# --- TCP-level fallout while the pfctl/iptables port-pair rules are up ---
# Both dugite (tokio) and cardano-node (network-mux) can surface a severed
# cross-group connection as an OS-level I/O error before either side's
# mini-protocol layer has classified it as a routine peer departure.
[Cc]onnection reset by peer
[Cc]onnection refused
[Bb]roken pipe
[Oo]s error 54
[Oo]s error 61
[Oo]s error 104
[Oo]s error 111

# --- ChainSync intersection / reconnect churn ---
# Expected on every reconnect attempt across a partitioned edge while the
# two sides' known-points lists no longer share a recent checkpoint — this
# is the routine "which point do we still have in common" negotiation, not
# a fault. Also covers the pre-existing #552/#908 stale-intersection class
# this round's healing step can retrigger.
MsgIntersectNotFound
[Nn]o intersection found
stale intersection

# --- Case 2's own fault: the permanent-fork / max-rollback refusal class ---
# This IS the condition rollback-round.sh Case 2 exists to provoke, and
# step 14 (expect_log_errors) positively REQUIRES at least one of these two
# lines to appear. Listed here too only so assert_no_other_errors never
# double-counts it as unexpected noise if either line's severity is ever
# bumped to ERROR. See rollback-round.sh step 14 for the full citation
# (crates/dugite-node/src/node/sync.rs and
# crates/dugite-storage/src/volatile_db.rs).
ChainSync intersection only at genesis
fork requires rollback beyond k

# --- cardano-node (Haskell) side of the same two contract outcomes ---
# ouroboros-network's tracer names for the analogous decisions on the
# Haskell nodes (cardano-bp, cardano-arbiter). SwitchedToAFork is the
# EXPECTED Case-1 reconvergence signal (rollback-round.sh step 7 asserts on
# it positively); ForkTooDeep/IntersectNotFound are Case 2's equivalents.
SwitchedToAFork
ForkTooDeep
IntersectNotFound
